
consider new validator api
// validator->validate($schema, $instance): array<violation> / obj(array<violation, getViolations, isValid)
// validator->assertValid($schema, $instance): void



may dynamicRef point to anchor?
YES:
{
  "$id": "https://json-schema.hyperjump.io/schema",
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "$dynamicRef": "#dynamic",
  "$defs": {
    "foo": {
      "$anchor": "dynamic",
      "type": "string"
    }
  }
}


may ref point to dynamicAnchor?
YES:
{
  "$id": "https://json-schema.hyperjump.io/schema",
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "$ref": "#dynamic",
  "$defs": {
    "foo": {
      "$dynamicAnchor": "dynamic",
      "type": "string"
    }
  }
}

if the value of $dynamicRef is not an anchor (#{anchor-identifier}) then should it behave as $ref?
what's "bookending requirement"?